      "He added: “After careful assessment of her general and cardiac fitness, she was deemed suitable for surgery and underwent bilateral trans-abdominal preperitoneal (TAPP) mesh repair, a minimally invasive laparoscopic procedure. Postoperatively, she was monitored in the ICU and then shifted to the ward. Oral intake was resumed on day one, and she recovered well. She was discharged in stable condition on postoperative day three and is doing well on follow-up.”",
