    excerpt: "While neonatal hernias are relatively common in preterm babies, Amyand\’s hernia is exceptionally rare. It affects only about 0.42% of these infants. The boy, born at just 28 weeks, underwent surgery on the 23rd day after his birth while under general anesthesia. Chennai, 12 September 2024: SRM Global Hospitals successfully performed a complex, three-part emergency ...",
